Z||000000||olliver||05-03-2001||04:43 PM||||Well i'm beyond the point of no return in my performance rebuild. (Not that i would want to stop anyways!!!)I've purchased the majority of parts that I need but there are still some that I don't have yet.  This is a list of everything that i've purchased.  NOTE: all prices are in C$ (for all my canuck brothers and sister)<P>towing fee: $40 (engine was blown)<BR>engine r/i: $250 (includes r/i of cradle)<BR>engine degreaser: $6<BR>poly cradle mounts: $85 **<BR>poly rear control arm bushings: $85 **<BR>2 rear c/a ball joints: $220<BR>4 cv boots: $60<BR>sandblast and repaint cradle w/endura: $50<BR>sandblast and repaint rear c/a's """ : $50<BR>2 tranny oil axle seals: $14.76<BR>trunk weather stripping: $121.41<BR>tranny pump seal: $16.95<BR>engine mount (oem style): $43.85<BR>2 tranny mounts (oem style): $58.85<BR>wire brush wheel: $10.49 (to clean tranny)<BR>can silver paint: $7.71 (to paint tranny)<BR>2.8L to a 3.4L w/210 hp: $3000 +/-<BR>being able to drive her once again......<BR>                                 PRICELESS<BR>** - includes shipping costs from the states<P>if anyone has any questions/info they would like to ask/add please do not hesitate....<BR>olliver<BR> <BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||thomas_l||05-03-2001||05:00 PM||||Hehe.. you were beyond the point of no return before the tow truck left your garage   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. My 87 GT project went from tow truck to racing in 3 weekends. Obviously I skipped a lot of the detail you did since I only needed to add a transmission (no pretty cradle or suspension parts). Lessseeeee.... I'm easing up on $2000 after getting the car for $400, trans, new clutch, rear whl bearings, brakes, 2 tires, align, cat (to pass smog), oil, filters, and a partridge in a pear tree. I agree with your last line - driving to the Fiero Factory last Saturday and then autocrossing Sunday was PRICELESS   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>By the way - how far along do you think you'll be by late July? I'll be in Edmonton 5 days for a wedding.<p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 05-03-2001).]||||reg||10
